.TH MU2EDAQ\-UPDATE\-SUBMODULES 1 "2026-07-23" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-update\-submodules \- fetch and fast-forward every submodule, then commit the pointer bumps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-update\-submodules.sh
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-commit ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-edit ]
.RI [ submodule\-path\ ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-update\-submodules.sh
fetches every submodule of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
meta-repository from its remote, fast-forwards each one that can be safely
advanced, and commits the resulting pointer changes in the parent repository
using the "Bump ..." message convention already used in this repo's history.
.PP
It is safe to run from a detached HEAD, from inside
.BR mu2edaq\-main ,
or from inside any submodule: each submodule is moved onto the branch it was
already tracking, or the remote's default branch if it was detached, before
being fast-forwarded. Submodules with local changes or history that has
diverged from
.RI origin/ branch
are left untouched and reported, never merged or rebased.
.PP
Unlike
.BR "mu2edaq\-bootstrap.sh update" ,
which unconditionally merges the remote tracking branch, this script only
ever fast-forwards, skips anything it cannot advance safely, and produces one
commit summarizing exactly which submodules moved and by how many commits.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.RI [ submodule\-path\ ... ]
Restrict the update to one or more submodules, named by the path shown in
.BR "git submodule status" .
With no arguments, every submodule is considered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Fetch only; report which submodules have commits available without changing
any checkout, staging anything, or committing.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-commit
Update and stage the affected submodule checkouts but stop short of
committing. Prints the
.B git commit
command to run afterwards.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-edit
Commit with the automatically generated message as-is instead of opening
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOR
.SS Selecting a branch
For each submodule already on a branch, that branch is fetched and
fast-forwarded. For a submodule in detached HEAD state, the script determines
the remote's default branch (via
.B origin/HEAD
if recorded, otherwise
.B "git ls\-remote \-\-symref origin HEAD" ,
falling back to
.BR main )
and checks that branch out, tracking
.RI origin/ branch ,
before fast-forwarding.
.SS Skip conditions
A submodule is left untouched, with a one-line reason printed, when: it is
not initialized; it has local uncommitted changes; its fetch fails; the
remote has no
.RI origin/ branch
matching the branch selected above; or the local branch has diverged from
.RI origin/ branch
such that a fast-forward merge is not possible.
.SS Commit message
When one submodule is bumped, the commit message is
.RI \(lq "Bump <name>: <branch>, <n> commit(s)" \(rq .
When several are bumped in one run, the message is a summary line followed
by one indented line per submodule, in the same format.
.SS Detached parent HEAD
If
.B mu2edaq\-main
itself is in detached HEAD state, a warning is printed before any work
starts: a bump commit created here will not be reachable from a branch until
you
.BR "git checkout \-b <name>" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The run completed (including the case where every submodule was already
up to date).
.TP
.B non-zero
Not run inside a git repository, or a later
.B git commit
failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview what would change across the whole suite:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-update\-submodules.sh \-\-dry\-run
.EE
Update everything and commit with the generated message:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-update\-submodules.sh
.EE
Update just one submodule:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-update\-submodules.sh mu2edaq\-controlcenter
.EE
Stage the bump but write the commit message yourself later:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-update\-submodules.sh \-\-no\-commit
    git commit
.EE
Non-interactive commit (no editor), e.g. from a script or cron job:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-update\-submodules.sh \-\-no\-edit
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .gitmodules
Defines the submodule paths and remote URLs used by this script.
Located at the root of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bootstrap (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-tag\-release (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-submodule (1),
.BR git\-merge (1)
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
.UE
